nd functional dimensions. This chapter aims at reviewing different classes of algorithms and highlighting several important dimensions of variation among them. Identifying these dimensions provides means for structuring a comprehensive taxonomy of approaches. We believe this exercise to be useful in working towards a general computational account of information-seeking. Such an account should facilitate the proposition of new hypotheses about information-seeking in humans and complement the existing psychological theory of curiosity."}, {"id": "https://openalex.org/W4283687550", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cognition.2022.105325", "title": "Curiosity as a Metacognitive Feeling", "publication_year": 2022, "type": "article", "cited_by_count": 89, "open_access": {"is_oa": true, "oa_status": "bronze", "oa_url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cognition.2022.105325", "any_repository_has_fulltext": tr

